From: Michael Podolszki <m.podolszki@phytec.de>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 15:20:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] bluetooth: btti_uart: tolerate line noise before the wakeup
 event

btti_uart registers its HCI device only after the BLE core has sent its
wakeup event (ff ff 02 04 2a 00 00), and the matcher insisted on the
receive buffer being exactly that: seven bytes, byte for byte.

On the phyVIP (CC33xx BDE-BW3351UP1 on lpuart5) the BLE core's TX line
comes up from low to idle-high right before that event, which the lpuart
delivers as a break and a handful of 0x00 bytes with a framing error. The
first buffer therefore reads

  00 00 00 00 ff ff 02 04 2a 00 00

and was rejected as "Unexpected wakeup pattern". Since the event is sent
exactly once per BLE_ENABLE, that left the driver in STATE_HW_ON with no
hci device until the next cold start -- rebinding the serdev does not
make the core repeat it.

Look for the pattern anywhere in the buffer instead and accept it when it
ends the buffer, so leading noise is skipped but anything following the
event is still treated as unexpected. Log how much noise was skipped.

Upstream-Status: Pending

Signed-off-by: Michael Podolszki <m.podolszki@phytec.de>
---
 drivers/bluetooth/btti_uart.c | 33 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++-------
 1 file changed, 26 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/bluetooth/btti_uart.c
+++ b/drivers/bluetooth/btti_uart.c
@@ -442,17 +442,34 @@
 	struct btti_uart_dev *bdev = serdev_device_get_drvdata(serdev);
 	const u8 hw_wakeup_evt[] = {HCI_VENDOR_PKT, 0xff, 0x02, 0x04, 0x2a, 0x00, 0x00};
 
+	size_t i;
+
 	if (count < sizeof hw_wakeup_evt)
 		return 0; // Reject data until all bytes have been received
 
-	if (count > sizeof hw_wakeup_evt)
-		goto error;
-
-	if (0 != memcmp(&hw_wakeup_evt, data, sizeof hw_wakeup_evt))
-		goto error;
-
-	btti_uart_sm_post_event(bdev, EVENT_HCI_WAKEUP_FRAME_RECEIVED);
-	return count;
+	/*
+	 * The wakeup event is the first thing the BLE core ever sends, and its
+	 * TX line comes up from low to idle-high right before it. On the phyVIP
+	 * that edge arrives as a break plus a few 0x00 bytes (framing error on
+	 * the lpuart), so the first buffer reads e.g.
+	 *   00 00 00 00 ff ff 02 04 2a 00 00
+	 * -- the exact pattern, preceded by line noise. The event is only sent
+	 * once per BLE_ENABLE; rejecting the buffer for its length means no HCI
+	 * device until the next cold start. Accept the pattern anywhere in the
+	 * buffer as long as it ends the buffer, i.e. nothing real follows it.
+	 */
+	for (i = 0; i + sizeof hw_wakeup_evt <= count; i++) {
+		if (memcmp(hw_wakeup_evt, data + i, sizeof hw_wakeup_evt))
+			continue;
+		if (i + sizeof hw_wakeup_evt != count)
+			goto error;
+		if (i)
+			dev_info(&serdev->dev,
+				 "wakeup event after %zu bytes of line noise",
+				 i);
+		btti_uart_sm_post_event(bdev, EVENT_HCI_WAKEUP_FRAME_RECEIVED);
+		return count;
+	}
 
 error:
 	dev_err(&serdev->dev, "Unexpected wakeup pattern");
